// Gobra contracts for domain types — F4.
//
// NewFollow refuses to construct a self-follow. This is the constructor
// that the service layer uses; the type system + this contract together
// make it impossible for a Follow{} value with a == b to enter the store.
//
// Stream 3 Phase 3: F4 is now discharged directly on the real
// `NewFollow` in dom.go (no `// @ trusted` marker on it). The two ghost
// stubs `GhostNewFollowOK` / `GhostNewFollowSelf` that previously sat
// here as proof scaffolding have been retired — the real function is
// now its own proof.
//
// Caller obligation: pass `isComparable(ErrSelfFollow)` as a
// precondition. `ErrSelfFollow` is a package-level `var` of interface
// type `error`, so Gobra cannot syntactically prove it is comparable
// without help. The dynamic type (`selfFollowError`) is a unit-value
// struct, so the assertion is trivially true at runtime.

package dom
